module utd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }
import frcrimp.deadlines.{ SentencingScheduled }

// The District of Utah's own criminal periods, counted under the criminal
// rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). No trigger carries a
// service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the manner of
// service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp and are only named
// here: a party communicates objections to the initial presentence report
// to the probation officer and the opposing party within 14 days after its
// disclosure (DUCrimR 32-1(a)(1); FRCrimP 32(f)(1)), and probation files
// the report with its addendum no fewer than 7 days before sentencing
// (DUCrimR 32-1(b)(1); FRCrimP 32(g)).
//
// Duties of court staff and other conditions that are not a party's
// deadline stay in notes: the courtroom deputy files documents the court
// considered at a detention or sentencing hearing within 3 days after it
// (DUCrimR 5-1; DUCrimR 32-1(b)(4), (5)); an unredacted transcript becomes
// available on PACER 90 days after it is filed, and the court reporter
// files the redacted transcript within 63 days after filing the original
// (DUCrimR 49.1-1(b)(2), (c)(3)). On appeal from a magistrate judge's
// misdemeanor or petty-offense order, an opening brief may not exceed 20
// pages or 6,200 words and a reply brief 10 pages or 3,100 words, unless a
// court order authorizes more (DUCrimR 58-2(c)); the corpus's limits are
// conjunctive, so these alternative limits are not encoded. There are no
// page limits for motions, memoranda, responses or replies (DUCrimR
// 12-1). An objection to a magistrate judge's order is governed by DUCivR
// 72-2 (DUCrimR 59-1), a civil rule this package does not bind.
//
// The earlier D. Utah criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A Notice of Supplemental Authority, or a response to one: at most 2
/// pages (DUCrimR 12-1(e)).
limit supplemental-authority { pages <= 2 cite "DUCrimR 12-1(e)" } cite "DUCrimR 12-1(e)"

/// The hearing at which a probation office report or document was
/// considered (DUCrimR 5-1).
event ReportHearingHeld()
/// A motion is served (DUCrimR 12-1(b)).
event MotionServed()
/// The memorandum opposing a motion is served (DUCrimR 12-1(c)).
event OppositionServed()
/// A Notice of Supplemental Authority is served (DUCrimR 12-1(e)).
event SupplementalAuthorityServed() paper supplemental-authority
/// The date set for the final pretrial conference (DUCrimR 16-1(c)).
event FinalPretrialConferenceScheduled()
/// A victim is served with notice of a motion for a subpoena for the
/// victim's personal or confidential information (DUCrimR 17-2(c)).
event VictimSubpoenaNoticeServed()
/// A party receives notice of an objection to the presentence report
/// (DUCrimR 32-1(a)(3)).
event PsrObjectionNoticed()
/// The date a seal is set to expire (DUCrimR 41-1(b), (c); 49.1-1(a)(2)).
event SealExpires()
/// A party receives notice that the court reporter has filed an original
/// transcript (DUCrimR 49.1-1(b), (c)).
event TranscriptFilingNoticed()
/// A magistrate judge's order in a misdemeanor or petty-offense case is
/// entered (DUCrimR 58-2(a)).
event PettyOrderEntered()
/// A notice of appeal from that order is filed (DUCrimR 58-2(b)(1)).
event PettyAppealNoticed()
/// The appellant's brief is served (DUCrimR 58-2(b)(2)).
event PettyAppellantBriefServed()
/// The appellee's brief is served (DUCrimR 58-2(b)(3)).
event PettyAppelleeBriefServed()

/// DUCrimR 5-1: an unrepresented defendant returns the copy of a
/// probation office report received to the probation officer within 7
/// days after the hearing where the report or document was considered.
deadline report-return: 7.days after ReportHearingHeld() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 5-1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 12-1(b): a response memorandum is filed within 14 days after
/// service of the motion.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 12-1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 12-1(c): the movant may file a reply memorandum, limited to
/// rebuttal, within 7 days after service of the memorandum opposing the
/// motion.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after OppositionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 12-1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 12-1(e)(2): if the court has not ruled, a party may file a
/// response of at most 2 pages within 7 days after service of a Notice of
/// Supplemental Authority; the court may decide the motion without waiting
/// for it.
deadline supplemental-authority-response: 7.days after SupplementalAuthorityServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 12-1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 16-1(c): unless the court orders otherwise, the parties
/// disclose case-in-chief experts 30 days before the final pretrial
/// conference by filing a notice of intent to use an expert.
deadline expert-disclosure: 30.days before FinalPretrialConferenceScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "DUCrimR 16-1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 17-2(c): a victim may file a sealed motion to quash or modify,
/// or otherwise object to, the subpoena within 14 days after service of
/// the notice; if none is filed, the movant files a certificate of
/// compliance and asks the court to direct issuance.
deadline victim-subpoena-objection: 14.days after VictimSubpoenaNoticeServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 17-2(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 32-1(a)(3): within 7 days after notice of an objection, the
/// parties and probation make reasonable efforts to resolve it.
deadline psr-objection-resolution: 7.days after PsrObjectionNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 32-1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 32-1(b)(2): no fewer than 7 days before sentencing, a party may
/// file a sentencing memorandum or Position of Party with Respect to
/// Sentencing Factors.
deadline sentencing-memorandum: 7.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 32-1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 32-1(b)(3): unless ordered otherwise, documents pertaining to
/// the defendant are provided to probation no later than 10 days before
/// the sentencing hearing.
deadline sentencing-documents-to-probation: 10.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "DUCrimR 32-1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 41-1(b): a motion to extend the seal of a FRCrimP 41 case and a
/// proposed order are presented to a magistrate judge at least 10 days
/// before the seal expires.
deadline seal-extension-motion: 10.days before SealExpires() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 41-1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 41-1(c): at least 10 days before the seal expires, the
/// government gives the Clerk's Office a copy of the FRCrimP 41 document
/// redacted as FRCrimP 49.1 requires.
deadline warrant-redacted-copy: 10.days before SealExpires() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 41-1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 49.1-1(a)(2): when a motion to unseal is granted or a seal is
/// set to expire, the filing party gives the Clerk's Office a copy redacting
/// the FRCrimP 49.1 personal identifiers at least 10 days before the seal
/// expires.
deadline unsealed-redacted-copy: 10.days before SealExpires() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 49.1-1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 49.1-1(b)(1): within 14 days after receiving notice that an
/// original transcript has been filed, each party reviews its portions
/// for personal identifiers.
deadline transcript-review: 14.days after TranscriptFilingNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 49.1-1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 49.1-1(c)(1): if redaction is required, a party files a Notice
/// of Intent to Request Redaction within 21 days after receiving notice
/// that the transcript has been filed.
deadline redaction-intent-notice: 21.days after TranscriptFilingNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 49.1-1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 49.1-1(c)(2): the Redaction Request, identifying page, line and
/// redaction, is filed within 42 days after receiving that notice.
deadline redaction-request: 42.days after TranscriptFilingNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 49.1-1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 58-2(a): a party appealing a magistrate judge's order in a
/// misdemeanor or petty-offense case to a district judge files and serves
/// a notice within 14 days after entry of the order.
deadline petty-appeal-notice: 14.days after PettyOrderEntered() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 58-2(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 58-2(b)(1): the appellant's brief is filed and served within 14
/// days after filing the notice of appeal.
deadline petty-appellant-brief: 14.days after PettyAppealNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 58-2(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 58-2(b)(2): the appellee's brief is filed and served within 14
/// days after service of the appellant's brief.
deadline petty-appellee-brief: 14.days after PettyAppellantBriefServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 58-2(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// DUCrimR 58-2(b)(3): the appellant may file and serve a reply brief
/// within 7 days after service of the appellee's brief.
deadline petty-reply-brief: 7.days after PettyAppelleeBriefServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "DUCrimR 58-2(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
